{"content":"Found the bug: `sqlparse.sql.Comparison.left` returns `self.tokens[1]` instead of `self.tokens[0]`. Since token index 0 is the left-hand operand and index 1 is typically whitespace, `comparison.left` was returning a whitespace token (str ' ') instead of the actual left operand (e.g. 'foo'), which exactly matches the reported failure `AssertionError: assert ' ' == 'foo'`. This affects every test that checks `.left` on a Comparison object - comparisons with keywords, floats, parenthesis, strings, functions, etc. Fixing the index to 0 resolves the regression.","tool_calls":[{"id":"fix_1","name":"replace_text","arguments":{"path":"sqlparse/sql.py","old_text":"    @property
    def left(self):
        return self.tokens[1]","new_text":"    @property
    def left(self):
        return self.tokens[0]"}}]}

